      "writtenOn": "2026-09-24T02:59:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "battery_get_disconnect_state() is called periodically. If the battery is permanently disconnected or if the wakeup command fails, this will repeatedly call board_wakeup_cutoff_battery() and spam the console logs on every invocation. Consider adding a state variable or flag to ensure this is only attempted once per disconnection event.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 505,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 505,
        "endChar": 0
      },
      "revId": "d77f9d166d41d0b6d5c20c97d0bd44efd1004ca6",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e09ed503_66cf4964",
        "filename": "common/battery_fuel_gauge.c",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 505,
      "author": {
        "id": 1442438
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-09-24T08:13:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "A single attempt may not be sufficient. If the wakeup command is interrupted by another battery command, the battery may fail to wake up. Periodic retries can improve the reliability of the battery wakeup process.\n\nOnce the battery wakes up successfully, the disconnected state will be cleared and the retries will stop. Therefore, we prefer to keep the current periodic retry mechanism and only optimize the logging if needed.",
      "parentUuid": "98de15c9_98441ddb",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 505,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 505,
        "endChar": 0
      },
